        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0863" n="727" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg727"/>

                <head>No. 525.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 29, 1888</date>.
                        (Received June 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 764.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction numbered 862,
                    of the 30th ultimo, I have the honorto inclose herewith copies of the note which
                    I addressed to the Marquis of Salisbury with respect to the correspondence
                    between Mr. Evarts and Sir Edward Thornton relative to the possessory right to
                    Christmas Island, and of his lordship’s reply to the same.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d525-a1.xml" xpointer="d525-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d525-a2.xml" xpointer="d525-a2"/>
